# Cloudflare Pages serves 404.html for any path that isn't a real static
# file — Vite's build only emits index.html at the root, so /practice,
# /daily, /rush, /browse, /legal, /challenge all 404 on a cold/direct load
# without this. Each real route is rewritten (200, not a redirect — the URL
# stays as typed) to the app shell so the SPA can boot and its own router
# takes it from there.
#
# The rewrite target is '/', not '/index.html': Cloudflare Pages
# canonicalizes '.html' URLs and 308-redirects '/index.html' to '/', which
# strips the original path and query string before the SPA's router ever
# sees them. Rewriting straight to '/' avoids that extra hop.
#
# No wildcard (`/* / 200`) on purpose: that would make every URL on the
# domain return 200 with the app shell, which is both bad for crawlers and
# breaks the "an unknown path returns a real 404" requirement. Anything
# not listed below keeps falling through to 404.html.
/practice / 200
/daily / 200
/rush / 200
/trace / 200
/browse / 200
/legal / 200
/settings / 200
# /challenge (v2 Phase 5c) is a *static* route — the whole challenge lives in
# the URL fragment (/challenge#<base64url>), which never reaches Cloudflare,
# so a plain literal line covers every possible challenge link. The fragment
# rides along through the rewrite untouched; App.tsx's own router reads it.
/challenge / 200
# /puzzle/:id (v2 Phase 1b) is the first *dynamic* route — Cloudflare's
# _redirects doesn't understand wouter's ':id' param syntax, only a glob
# ('*'), so this is scoped to /puzzle/* rather than a literal per-id line
# (which would be infinite anyway). A bare /puzzle/ (no id) still matches
# this glob and rewrites to the app shell — App.tsx's router then falls
# through to its ordinary "Nothing here" catch-all for that case, same as
# any other path the client-side router doesn't recognize; a truly unknown
# top-level path (e.g. /nonsense) still isn't covered by any rule here and
# keeps 404ing for real.
/puzzle/* / 200
